rac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+3x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{{x}^{2}-2xy+{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{{2}^{3}-3({2}^{2})(2)+3(2)({2}^{2})-{2}^{3}}{{2}^{2}-2(2)(2)+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-24+24-8}{4-8+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+3x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{{x}^{2}-2xy+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{(x-y)^{3}}{(x-y)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{(x-y)(x-y)^{2}}{(x-y)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{(x-y)\\cancel{(x-y)^{2}}}{\\cancel{(x-y)^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,2)}(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,2)}(x-y) & =2-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $0.$" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315877 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315878 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315879 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315880 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315881 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1041 "selection" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315880 13194139534866 true] [17592186315876 1110 #uuid "08e5b09e-79d3-555b-b694-c46828149e88" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315877 1034 "2" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315877 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534866 true] [17592186315877 1111 #uuid "039139d6-3863-589d-a57e-e00d46b79bd2" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315878 1034 "1" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534866 true] [17592186315878 1111 #uuid "32dc1ec0-f7fe-56cd-8b45-ff7b6db19dd8" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315879 1034 "-4" 13194