Find ${lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{x+y-{z}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+y}-z}.$" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315889 1113 #uuid "045f5f9b-4b8b-5043-84f1-251aa8dc17e0" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315889 1145 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{x+y-{z}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+y}-z} & =\\frac{1+0-{1}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+0}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+0-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{x+y-{z}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+y}-z} & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{(x+y-{z}^{2})(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)}{(\\sqrt{x+y}-z)(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{(x+y-{z}^{2})(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)}{x+y-{z}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{\\cancel{(x+y-{z}^{2})}(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)}{\\cancel{x+y-{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,0,1)}(\\sqrt{x+y}+z) & =\\sqrt{1+0}+1 \\\\  & =1+0+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $2.$" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315891 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315892 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315893 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315894 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315895 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1041 "selection" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315892 13194139534866 true] [17592186315890 1110 #uuid "33d25667-e284-58be-bb98-5b7e6f28de6b" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315891 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315891 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139