,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{0}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2({0}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is also true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{3\\cancel{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315898 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315899 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315900 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315901 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315902 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1041 "selection" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315898 13194139534866 true] [17592186315897 1110 #uuid "9028a2e5-c466-504a-a3b9-55e0b6cd9b16" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315898 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534866 true] [17592186315898 1111 #uuid "b13a23a3-44bd-5c62-8a5e-06552f88d23b" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315899 1034 "II and III only" 13194