rue] [17592186315952 1113 #uuid "c00255c1-b43f-541c-9a67-c83b1ddf6f8c" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315952 1145 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}=\\frac{(-1)^{2}+2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1+{1}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{(x+y)^{2}}{(y-x)(y+x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{(x+y)(x+y)}{(y-x)(x+y)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{x+y}{y-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{x+y}{y-x} & =\\frac{(-1)+1}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $0.$" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315954 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315955 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315956 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315957 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315958 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1041 "selection" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315957 13194139534866 true] [17592186315953 1110 #uuid "b60bdedf-738a-5f0f-a06d-1e0d0ce7b04b" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315954 1034 "2" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315954 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534866 true] [17592186315954 1111 #uuid "16a48cfc-2c20-50da-b9f5-03734c029ecd" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315955 1034 "1" 13194139534866 true] [17592186315955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534866 true] [17592186315955 1111 #uuid "d5165c9b-7a8a-5914-